opennyai_summary.facts:
The present criminal revision has been filed to quash the order dated 28.2.2023 passed by Special Judge, POCSO Act/ Additional District and Sessions Judge, Aligarh, in Criminal Appeal No. 19 of 2023 in Case Crime No. 38 of 2022, under Sections 363, 342, 376 I.P.C. and 5/6 POCSO Act, Police Juvenile X vs State Of Up Through Principal Secretary ... on 10 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/37957213/
1 Station Roravar, District Aligarh.
Learned counsel for the revisionist submits:
( i) admittedly, the revisionist was a juvenile, aged about 17 years, two months and two days, on the date of alleged incident.
He is in child protection home since 29.1.2022;
(ii) the revisionist has been falsely implicated;
(iii) there is no specific or strong objection raised in the DPO report, other than the general and vague observations;
(iv) there is no criminal history of the revisionist;
(v) there is no hope of early conclusion of the trial;
(vi) the revisionist has remained confined in the child observation home for an unduly long period of time;
(vii) none of the grounds contemplated under section 12 of the Juvenile Justice (Care and Protection of Children) Act, 2000 (hereinafter referred to as the Act) are available, to deny the bail to the revisionist.
